[?2004l   382	Stakeholder workshop #901 on intercompany netting dispute produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.
   383	
   384	## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing
   385	
   386	The March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance
   387	messages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes
   388	`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or
   389	equal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,
   390	apply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply
   391	after ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.
   392	
   393	## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing — supporting chronology
   394	
   395	Privacy review #424 redacted personal data from treasury wire cutoff failures threads but retained transaction identifiers needed for reconciliation testing.
   396	
   397	Grant compliance WP-5555 tied treasury wire cutoff failures attestation gaps to hold flag suppression visible only when hold flags used corrected rather than pre-correction ledger dates.
